---
// Required on a live site. Google Ads and Meta both refuse a landing page with
// no privacy policy, and the form collects real contact details.
// The collected-data list is generated from site.formCollects so it can never
// drift out of step with the actual form.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
const updated = '24 August 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${site.legalName} handles the details you send through the enquiry form. Short version: they go to Daniel's inbox and nowhere else.`}
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow label">
        <span>Privacy</span>
        <span class="head-dim">&middot; Updated {updated}</span>
      </p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="short">
          Short version: the enquiry form goes to my inbox. I do not sell anything to
          anyone, I do not add you to a mailing list, and there are no advertising
          cookies on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Who this is</h2>
        <p>
          This site is run by {site.legalName} ({site.owner}), based in {site.base}.
          You can reach me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or
          on <a href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What the form collects</h2>
        <p>If you fill in the enquiry form, it sends me:</p>
        <ul>{site.formCollects.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>
          Nothing is required beyond what is marked required on the form itself, and there
          are no hidden fields collecting anything else.
        </p>

        <h2>What I do with it</h2>
        <p>
          I read it, I reply to it, and if it looks like a fit I build you a demo. That is
          the entire use. Form submissions are handled by Netlify, who host this site, and
          they land in my email. I do not sell, rent or share your details with anyone, and
          nothing you send is used to train anything.
        </p>

        <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiries stay in my email and in Netlify's form records so I have a history of
          what we discussed. Ask me to delete yours and I will, and I will confirm when it
          is done.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets no advertising cookies and runs no tracking pixels. If analytics
          is running it is Plausible, which is cookieless and does not collect anything
          that identifies you personally. Netlify keeps standard server logs, as every web
          host does.
        </p>

        <h2>Other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Some links go to sites I have built for other people, or to demo builds. Once you
          are on one of those, this policy stops applying.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask me what I hold about you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete
          it. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and I will sort it
          out. If you are not happy with how I have handled it you can complain to the
          Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at oaic.gov.au.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this changes I will update the date at the top. It was last updated
          on {updated}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 {
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 110, 'wght' 650;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 2vw, 23px); letter-spacing: -.012em;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }
  .prose p { color: var(--on-light-soft); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0 0 16px 0; display: grid; gap: 7px; }
  .prose li { position: relative; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--on-light-soft); font-size: 15.5px; }
  .prose li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .58em; width: 8px; height: 8px; background: var(--amber); }
  .short {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber); padding: 14px 18px;
    background: var(--linen); color: var(--ink) !important; font-size: 16px;
  }
</style>
